A||||34||fldevel||how many miles am i supposed to get to a full tank of gas ??||||1||
Z||000000||fldevel||02-06-2001||01:22 PM|||| i drive a 85GT as many of you already know ..never really payed much attention to my gas milage till it seemed like it was sucking up more gas than normal .. lately ive been getting around 100 miles to a tank of gas depending on how i drive is this good ? also it seems to suck up more gas when i put 93 oct in .. why ??||||reg||1
Z||000001||LarryB||02-06-2001||01:28 PM||||Unless you're doing all stop-and-go driving you should be getting at least double that.  I get 22-23 MPG in mixed driving with my 4 speed, 29-30 highway. You didn't say if you had a 4 speed or auto, with auto you might get a couple of MPG less. <P>That sound from the 93 octane isn't the additional gas being used, its the additional money being vacuumed from your wallet.  You don't need 93 octane unless maybe if you've got a turbo. <BR>||||reg||4
Z||000002||fierojunky||02-06-2001||01:30 PM||||Sounds like your getting terrible mileage.  I get about 180-200 miles a tank with my 87SE.  Also i live in PA with alot more hills and stuff than florida.  ||||reg||13
Z||000003||fldevel||02-06-2001||01:38 PM|||| its a 4 sp ..but when i fill the tank up  and reset the tripomiter im usualy looking for a gas station at about 95-100 miles whares all the gas goin ?? ||||reg||1
Z||000004||DavidHenshaw||02-06-2001||01:40 PM||||Is that a V6? <P>My 2.8 V6 gets about 24 mpg highway and about 19-20 mpg in town. It sounds like you're geting about half that much. Of course a four banger gets better milage than a V6. <P>You can check your milage by filling the tank to the top the next time you buy gas, set the trip odometer to zero, drive until the tank is 3/4 or more used up and then again fill the gas tank to the top. Then divide the number of miles you have traveled by the number of gallons required to refil the tank.<P>Example: 195 miles traveled divided by 9.5 gallons to fill the tank would give you 20.5 miles per gallon. <P>If your tank holds 10 to 11 gallons and you're only going about 100 miles each time then your milage is more like a big SUV than a Fiero. <P>Dave<P>86 GT ||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||02-06-2001||01:58 PM||||i get between 150-175 to a fill up. V6 turbo 4 spd. I only use 87 octane. Once in a while 89||||reg||1
Z||000006||TheFiero64||02-06-2001||02:04 PM||||I get around 190-200 on a tank in my 88 coupe v6 5 speed.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||10
Z||000007||Oreif||02-06-2001||02:10 PM||||I have a V-6 with an automatic trans. I get about 160-200 miles per tank. I generally fill-up when I'm at 1/4 tank and the trip odometer is usually at 160 miles. That is combined driving (highway/city) I usually get about 18 city and 22 highway as an average. When you fill up how much gas do you put in? how correct is the gas gage?||||reg||1
Z||000008||fldevel||02-06-2001||02:10 PM||||ok .. so what could be my problem here .. car is running excelent fireing on all 6...what would cause it to use more gas ??<BR>also orif .. dont really know how correct it is .. but when at 1/4 tank it takes about 9 bux to fill it up <p>[This message has been edited by fldevel (edited 02-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||jerpro||02-06-2001||02:33 PM||||Do you have a snapon? or a paul mitchell system?<BR>If not your friend probably has one. check on obd2 for your O2 sensor, it may have gone bad, also check the fuel filter, it may be clogged up, also, check for vaccum leaks, although not noticeable you might be loosing power which makes you step on the gas harder and thus, more gas consumption.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Only try your best, and if at first you don't succeed... TRY HARDER.||||reg||1
Z||000010||1FST2M6||02-06-2001||03:02 PM||||LMAO!! hehe Paul Mitchell.. heh! <P>Mitchel on demand and the Snap-on DVDs are a good place to start... the Fuel canister near the air filter.. that maybe shot, is your egr working right.. the O2 sensor.. how many miles does it have on it? have you ever had the injectors cleaned? is every stop light you come to, a race with the driver next to you even if he's not racing you?  (you'd be suprised at how many people really drive like that... they come into the shop everyday)  my $.02   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||Carrolles||02-06-2001||04:37 PM||||Your mileage may not be as bad as you think.  You said you use 93 octane gas and it takes about $9.00 to re-fill after about 100 miles.<P>Lets assume you pay around $1.60 per gallon for the 93 octane gas.  That means you've used 5.625 gallons to go 100 miles.  This works out to 17.77 mpg.  Not great but if you are hard on your car that could be reasonable.<P>I drive an 85 SE v-6 4spd pretty conservatively (at least since my last ticket).  I get around 22 to 24 mpg on my commute to work on mountain backroads driving basically 50 mph.  On the way to Daytona I got as much as 28.5 mpg pure highway driving at 75 mph.<P>Next time you fill up make a note of the actual gallons used, not the $ used and calculate the actual mileage you're getting.  Fiero gas gauges aren't the most accurate or precise.  I usually pay more attention to the trip odometer ( I always reset it to zero when I fill up) than the gas gauge.<P>What trans do you have?  If it is auto are you sure the TCC is locking up?  My 85GT Auto TCC is unplugged for now and the mileage reflects it.  If it is a 4spd do you notice any clutch slippage lately?  Have you checked your timing lately?<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll<p>[This message has been edited by Carrolles (edited 02-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||loafer87gt||02-06-2001||05:07 PM||||I usually get around 375-400 km out of a tank of gas||||reg||1
Z||000013||FLASHY||02-06-2001||05:17 PM||||I have a manual V-6 and I tend to get around 310 - 340 km on a tank of regular gas. That works out to approx. 194 - 212 miles per tank (or am I wrong?). I also tend to drive it quite hard most the time. Funny, for some reason I always thought that wasn't very good for a Fiero but by the looks of it, it seems quite normal. Well whata ya know.||||reg||1
