Z||000015||Motorhead||02-06-2001||05:48 PM||||WHOA! 120 miles/tank with the Duke?  You must have one of those Gremlins sitting in the tank with a straw drinking it all!<BR>I don't really watch my mileage very closely because my gas stops are so infrequent.  But I do know that I run somewhere around 280 miles per fill-up, and that's filling when still showing just under 1/4 tank or better. <P>------------------<BR>"The one who dies with the most toys wins!"<BR>  bluewater46@hotmail.com<BR>1986 coupe<BR>1984 coupe<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1372350&a=10234998&p=38686771&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||fldevel||02-06-2001||10:59 PM||||filled her up today and took a drive to ocala .. about a 45 min drive from here and back .. then drove it around my home town running some errands and managed to squeeze 150 miles on the tripomiter with like 1/8 tank left ..  also car idles a little high in cold weather till it warms up ..is that normal too ..<P>and also it taked forever for the heater to start working.. i drive up to 10 miles freezing to death cause my car dosent heat up untill ive drivin it for an hour ..and yes there is a thermastat in it ..<P>i should probibly be posting these in the tech chat room rather than in here hua ??<P>thaks for the space .. ||||reg||1
Z||000017||Cooter||02-06-2001||11:47 PM||||I am going to guess that your thermostat is not up to the standard 195 degrees. If it is taking a long time to warm up then you are running in open loop -warm up mode, and will run richer. My 3.4/4.10's gets about 190-210 miles on a 10 gallon fill up. This is with mostly in town miles.||||reg||1
Z||000018||Carrolles||02-07-2001||08:38 AM||||Is the O-ring on the thermostat in good shape?  If it is cut or missing then coolant is by-passing the t-stat and contributing to the too cool running.||||reg||1
